<!-- patchy:runner-image -->
### Agent runner image
{{ if .NotApplicable }}
patchy did not use `{{ .Manifest }}` to choose the image the agent runs in:
{{ fence .Reason }}
The agent ran in the default runner image instead, which carries no language toolchain. Nothing else about this finding
changes.

**To run the agent in your own image**, publish it prebuilt and name it in `image`, or declare it in
`.patchy/agent.yaml`, which takes precedence. {{ code "patchy check image <ref>" }} runs patchy's checks on an image
before you declare it, and the [agent image guide]({{ .GuideURL }}) covers what the image needs.
{{- else if .Rejected }}
patchy could not use {{ if .Declared }}{{ code .Declared }}, declared in{{ else }}the declaration in{{ end }} `{{ .Manifest }}` (`{{ .Rejected }}`):
{{ fence .Reason }}
{{- if .Parked }}
patchy parked this finding for a human rather than run it on another image, because the operator set
`onReject: handoff`. Comment {{ code .ApproveCommand }} to run it in the default runner image.
{{- else }}
The agent ran in the default runner image instead, which carries no language toolchain.
{{- end }}

**How to fix it:** correct the image or `{{ .Manifest }}`, then run {{ code (printf "patchy check image %s" .CheckRef) }},
which runs every check patchy runs and reports each verdict. The
[troubleshooting table]({{ .GuideURL }}#troubleshooting) gives the fix for `{{ .Rejected }}`. patchy reads the
declaration once per finding, so the fix applies to the next finding on this repository.
{{- else }}
`{{ .Manifest }}` declares {{ code .Declared }}. patchy pinned it to {{ code .Image }}{{ if .Verified }}, verified its
signature{{ end }}, and runs the agent in it with patchy's own tools added under `/patchy/bin`.
{{- with .Incompatible }}

The {{ .Stage }} (attempt {{ .Attempt }}) stopped before the agent started: the image failed the agent's preflight
(`image_incompatible`):
{{ fence .Detail }}
The image must be glibc-based, have `bash`, `sh` and `git` on its `PATH`, and let uid 65532 run them.
{{ code (printf "patchy check image %s --run" $.CheckRef) }} runs the same preflight in a local container.
{{- end }}
{{- with .SandboxRefused }}

The {{ .Stage }} (attempt {{ .Attempt }}) was refused before the agent started (`SandboxUnenforced`): the cluster does
not enforce the network isolation patchy requires before it runs a repository-declared image. This is not a problem
with your image; until an operator enables NetworkPolicy enforcement and restarts the controllers, this finding runs in
the default runner image.
{{- end }}

To change the image, edit `{{ .Manifest }}`; the [agent image guide]({{ .GuideURL }}) covers what the image needs.
{{- end }}
